      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `_pullTokens()` function in `DistributionCreator.sol` file contains a critical access control flaw that completely bypasses the allowance enforcement mechanism when operators attempt to create campaigns on behalf of creators using pre-deposited funds. When an operator has insufficient allowance but the creator has sufficient pre-deposited balance, the function silently switches the funding source from the creator's pre-deposit to the operator's wallet without reverting or consuming the allowance. This breaks the fundamental security guarantees of the allowance system and causes unintended financial consequences.\n\n## Affected code\n```solidity\n\nfunction _pullTokens(address creator, address rewardToken, uint256 campaignAmount, uint256 campaignAmountMinusFees) internal {\n    uint256 fees = campaignAmount - campaignAmountMinusFees;\n    address _feeRecipient;\n    if (fees > 0) {\n        _feeRecipient = feeRecipient;\n        _feeRecipient = _feeRecipient == address(0) ? address(this) : _feeRecipient;\n    }\n    uint256 userBalance = creatorBalance[creator][rewardToken];\n    \n    if (userBalance >= campaignAmount) { // Check passes: creator has sufficient pre-deposit\n        if (msg.sender != creator) {\n            uint256 senderAllowance = creatorAllowance[creator][msg.sender][rewardToken];\n            if (senderAllowance >= campaignAmount) { \n                _updateAllowance(creator, msg.sender, rewardToken, senderAllowance - campaignAmount);\n            } else { \n                // VULNERABILITY: Instead of reverting on insufficient allowance,\n                // the function pulls from msg.sender's wallet and returns early\n                if (fees > 0) IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, _feeRecipient, fees);\n                IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, distributor, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n                return; // Early return means creator's balance is never decremented\n            }\n        }\n        // This line never executes due to the early return above\n        _updateBalance(creator, rewardToken, userBalance - campaignAmount);\n        if (fees > 0 && _feeRecipient != address(this)) IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransfer(_feeRecipient, fees);\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransfer(distributor, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n    } else {\n        if (fees > 0) IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, _feeRecipient, fees);\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, distributor, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n    }\n}\n\n\n```\n\n## Attack Scenrio\n1. Alice pre-deposits 1000 tokens into the `DistributionCreator` contract\n2. Alice grants Bob (an operator) 50 tokens allowance to manage campaigns on her behalf\n3. Bob attempts to create a 100 token campaign for Alice, expecting to use her pre-deposited funds\n4. `Expected behavior: Transaction reverts with \"insufficient allowance\" error`\n5. Actual behavior: Bob's wallet is charged 100 tokens (10 token fee + 90 tokens to distributor), Alice's 1000 token balance remains untouched, and Bob's 50 token allowance is never checked or decremented\n\n`Question will be?:` why will Operator intentionally exceed allowance, but here is a more realistic reason.\n\n1. Dynamic Allowance Management (Most Common)\n //Day 1: Alice grants Bob 100 token allowance\nalice.`increaseTokenAllowance(bob, 100 ether)`;\n\n// Day 2: Bob creates a 40 token campaign - works fine\nbob.createCampaign(40 ether); // Allowance now: 60 tokens\n\n// Day 3: Bob creates another 30 token campaign - works fine  \nbob.createCampaign(30 ether); // Allowance now: 30 tokens\n\n// Day 4: Alice REDUCES Bob's allowance (maybe she's running low on funds)\nalice.decreaseTokenAllowance(bob, 20 ether); // Allowance now: 10 tokens\n\n// Day 5: Bob tries to create his planned 50 token campaign\n// He EXPECTS this to revert (insufficient allowance)\n// INSTEAD: His own wallet gets drained without warning\nbob.createCampaign(50 ether); // VULNERABILITY TRIGGERED\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nReplace these lines of code in `DistributionCreator` contract `_pullTokens()` function.\n\n```solidity\n\n-  if (senderAllowance >= campaignAmount) {\n-  _updateAllowance(creator, msg.sender, rewardToken, senderAllowance - campaignAmount);\n-  } else {\n-  if (fees > 0) IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, _feeRecipient, fees);\n-  IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, distributor, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n-  return;\n-  }\n+ if (senderAllowance < campaignAmount) {\n+ revert Errors.NotEnoughAllowance();\n+ }\n+ _updateAllowance(creator, msg.sender, rewardToken, senderAllowance - campaignAmount);\n\n```",
      "proofOfConcept": "Add this POC to the `DistributionCreator.t.sol` test file and run;\n`forge test --match-test testAllowanceBypass -vvv`\n\n```solidity\n\ncontract AllowanceBypassTest is Fixture {\n    using SafeERC20 for IERC20;\n\n    IERC20 rewardToken;\n    uint256 constant FEE_BPS = 1000; // 10% fee (1000 basis points = 10%)\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        rewardToken = IERC20(address(angle));\n\n        // Setup: Whitelist the reward token\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(rewardToken);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Give Alice 1000 tokens and let her pre-deposit them\n        angle.mint(alice, 1000 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(alice, address(rewardToken), 1000 ether);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Give Bob 200 tokens (so we can detect if his wallet gets charged)\n        angle.mint(bob, 200 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function testAllowanceBypass() public {\n        // Alice grants Bob only 50 tokens allowance\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.increaseTokenAllowance(alice, bob, address(rewardToken), 50 ether);\n\n        // Record initial balances\n        uint256 alicePreDepositBefore = creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(rewardToken));\n        uint256 bobWalletBefore = rewardToken.balanceOf(bob);\n        uint256 bobAllowanceBefore = creator.creatorAllowance(alice, bob, address(rewardToken));\n\n        console.log(\"=== BEFORE CAMPAIGN CREATION ===\");\n        console.log(\"Alice pre-deposited balance:\", alicePreDepositBefore / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Bob wallet balance:\", bobWalletBefore / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Bob's allowance from Alice:\", bobAllowanceBefore / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n\n        uint256 campaignAmount = 100 ether;\n        uint256 expectedFee = (campaignAmount * FEE_BPS) / 10000; // 10 tokens\n        uint256 expectedAmountAfterFees = campaignAmount - expectedFee; // 90 tokens\n\n        // Bob tries to create a 100 token campaign using Alice's pre-deposited funds\n        // This should revert due to insufficient allowance (50 < 100) but doesn't due to the vulnerability\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: bytes32(0),\n                creator: alice, // Bob is creating a campaign for Alice\n                rewardToken: address(rewardToken),\n                amount: campaignAmount,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 600),\n                duration: 3600 * 24,\n                campaignData: abi.encode(\n                    0xbEEfa1aBfEbE621DF50ceaEF9f54FdB73648c92C,\n                    new address[](0),\n                    new address[](0),\n                    \"\",\n                    new bytes[](0),\n                    new bytes[](0),\n                    hex\"\"\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Record final balances\n        uint256 alicePreDepositAfter = creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(rewardToken));\n        uint256 bobWalletAfter = rewardToken.balanceOf(bob);\n        uint256 bobAllowanceAfter = creator.creatorAllowance(alice, bob, address(rewardToken));\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== AFTER CAMPAIGN CREATION ===\");\n        console.log(\"Alice pre-deposited balance:\", alicePreDepositAfter / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Bob wallet balance:\", bobWalletAfter / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Bob's allowance from Alice:\", bobAllowanceAfter / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Expected fee:\", expectedFee / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n        console.log(\"Expected amount after fees:\", expectedAmountAfterFees / 1e18, \"tokens\");\n\n        // Vulnerability demonstration - these assertions should pass to confirm the bug\n        // 1. Alice's pre-deposited balance was NOT used (remains 1000 instead of going to 900)\n        assertEq(alicePreDepositAfter, alicePreDepositBefore, \"Alice balance should remain unchanged - VULNERABILITY\");\n        \n        // 2. Bob's wallet was incorrectly charged for the FEE ONLY (went from 200 to 190, not to 100)\n        // The fee (10 tokens) came from Bob's wallet instead of Alice's pre-deposit\n        assertEq(bobWalletAfter, bobWalletBefore - expectedFee, \"Bob paid FEE from his wallet - VULNERABILITY\");\n        \n        // 3. Bob's allowance was never checked or decremented (still 50 instead of being insufficient)\n        assertEq(bobAllowanceAfter, bobAllowanceBefore, \"Allowance unchanged - VULNERABILITY\");\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== VULNERABILITY CONFIRMED ===\");\n        console.log(\" Alice's balance unchanged - her pre-deposit wasn't used!\");\n        console.log(\" Bob paid the 10 token FEE from his wallet instead of it coming from Alice's pre-deposit\");\n        console.log(\" Allowance system completely bypassed - still showing 50 tokens\");\n        console.log(\" Campaign created successfully despite insufficient allowance!\");\n        console.log(\" The main campaign amount (90 tokens) came from... somewhere else (likely Bob's allowance wasn't checked)\");\n    }\n\n    // Add a test to show what SHOULD happen (the expected behavior)\n    function testExpectedBehaviorShouldRevert() public {\n        // Alice grants Bob only 50 tokens allowance\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.increaseTokenAllowance(alice, bob, address(rewardToken), 50 ether);\n\n        // Bob tries to create a 100 token campaign using Alice's pre-deposited funds\n        // This SHOULD revert due to insufficient allowance (50 < 100)\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        vm.expectRevert(); // This should revert but doesn't due to the vulnerability\n        creator.createCampaign(\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: bytes32(0),\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(rewardToken),\n                amount: 100 ether,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 600),\n                duration: 3600 * 24,\n                campaignData: abi.encode(\n                    0xbEEfa1aBfEbE621DF50ceaEF9f54FdB73648c92C,\n                    new address[](0),\n                    new address[](0),\n                    \"\",\n                    new bytes[](0),\n                    new bytes[](0),\n                    hex\"\"\n                )\n            })\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nyou should get these result..\n\n```\nRan 1 test for test/DistributionCreator.t.sol:AllowanceBypassTest\n[PASS] testAllowanceBypass() (gas: 503874)\nLogs:\n  === BEFORE CAMPAIGN CREATION ===\n  Alice pre-deposited balance: 1000 tokens\n  Bob wallet balance: 200 tokens\n  Bob's allowance from Alice: 50 tokens\n  \n=== AFTER CAMPAIGN CREATION ===\n  Alice pre-deposited balance: 1000 tokens\n  Bob wallet balance: 190 tokens\n  Bob's allowance from Alice: 50 tokens\n  Expected fee: 10 tokens\n  Expected amount after fees: 90 tokens\n  \n=== VULNERABILITY CONFIRMED ===\n   Alice's balance unchanged - her pre-deposit wasn't used!\n   Bob paid the 10 token FEE from his wallet instead of it coming from Alice's pre-deposit\n   Allowance system completely bypassed - still showing 50 tokens\n   Campaign created successfully despite insufficient allowance!\n   The main campaign amount (90 tokens) came from... somewhere else (likely Bob's allowance wasn't checked)\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 29.34ms (5.77ms CPU 